= Decision theory =

This category groups knowledge on decisions under uncertainty, preferences, utilities, risk, heuristics and systematic departures from idealized choice models. It is a '''browse category''', not an additional BITwiki controlled [[Property:Domain|Domain]].

== Scope ==
Includes formal [[Decision theory]], [[Prospect theory]], [[Bounded rationality]], [[Satisficing]], [[Loss aversion]], the [[Decoy effect]], and related judgment research. A page may be cross-classified when it substantively connects mathematics, cognition, governance or economics.

